ToolSpecification.description:
Add a review comment to a Gerrit change following Gerrit API REST spec.

        Args:
            url: URL of the Gerrit review
            message: General summary comment
            labels: Code review evaluation labels with values:
                - Code-Review: -2 (Do not submit), -1 (I would prefer this is not submitted),
                  +1 (Looks good to me, but someone else must approve), +2 (Looks good to me, approved)
            robot_comments: Per-file robot comments dict following Gerrit 3.8.9 API.
            comments: Per-file human comments dict following Gerrit 3.8.9 API.
                Schema: Dict[str, List[RobotCommentInfo]] where:
                - Key: file path (string)
                - Value: List of RobotCommentInfo objects

                RobotCommentInfo schema:
                {
                  "robot_id": str,           # Required: Robot identifier
                  "robot_run_id": str,       # Required: Robot run identifier
                  "message": str,            # Required: Comment message
                  "line": int,               # Optional: Line number for line comments
                  "range": {                 # Optional: Range for multi-line comments
                    "start_line": int,
                    "start_character": int,
                    "end_line": int,
                    "end_character": int
                  },
                  "fix_suggestions": [       # Optional: Array of fix suggestions
                    {
                      "description": str,     # Required: Fix description
                      "replacements": [       # Required: Array of replacements
                        {
                          "path": str,        # Required: File path
                          "range": {...},     # Required: Range to replace
                          "replacement": str  # Required: Replacement text
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }

                Example:
                {
                  "path/to/file.java": [
                    {
                      "robot_id": "linter-bot",
                      "robot_run_id": "run-123",
                      "message": "[nit] trailing whitespace",
                      "line": 23,
                    },
                    {
                      "robot_id": "formatter-bot",
                      "robot_run_id": "run-456",
                      "message": "Incorrect indentation",
                      "range": {"start_line": 50, "start_character": 0, "end_line": 55, "end_character": 20},
                      "fix_suggestions": [
                        {
                          "description": "Fix indentation to 4 spaces",
                          "replacements": [
                            {
                              "path": "path/to/file.java",
                              "range": {"start_line": 50, "start_character": 0, "end_line": 55, "end_character": 20},
                              "replacement": "    properly indented code"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }

        Robot Comment Fields (Gerrit 3.8.9 API):
            - robot_id: (required) Identifier of the robot that generated the comment
            - robot_run_id: (required) Identifier of the robot run that generated the comment
            - message: (required) The comment message
            - path: File path (automatically set from dict key)
            - line: Line number for line comments
            - range: Range for multi-line comments with start_line, start_character, end_line, end_character
            - fix_suggestions: Array of FixSuggestionInfo objects

        Examples:
            # Simple approval
            labels={"Code-Review": +2}

            # Robot comments with fix suggestions
            message="Automated code review completed"
            labels={"Code-Review": -1}
            robot_comments={
              "src/main.py": [
                {
                  "robot_id": "code-analyzer",
                  "robot_run_id": "analysis-2024-001",
                  "message": "Fix typo in variable name",
                  "line": 42,
                  "fix_suggestions": [
                    {
                      "description": "Rename 'varialbe' to 'variable'",
                      "replacements": [
                        {
                          "path": "src/main.py",
                          "range": {"start_line": 42, "start_character": 8, "end_line": 42, "end_character": 16},
                          "replacement": "variable"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }

        Comments Fields (Gerrit 3.8.9 API):
            - message: (required) The comment message
            - line: Line number for line comments
            - range: Range for multi-line comments with start_line, start_character, end_line, end_character
            - unresolved: Mark comment as unresolved (requires attention)

        Comments Schema: Dict[str, List[CommentInfo]] where:
        - Key: file path (string)
        - Value: List of CommentInfo objects

        CommentInfo schema:
        {
          "message": str,            # Required: Comment message
          "line": int,               # Optional: Line number for line comments
          "range": {                 # Optional: Range for multi-line comments
            "start_line": int,
            "start_character": int,
            "end_line": int,
            "end_character": int
          },
          "unresolved": bool         # Optional: Mark comment as unresolved
        }

        Example:
        {
          "path/to/file.java": [
            {
              "message": "This needs to be refactored",
              "line": 23,
              "unresolved": true
            },
            {
              "message": "Consider using a more descriptive variable name",
              "range": {"start_line": 50, "start_character": 0, "end_line": 55, "end_character": 20}
            }
          ]
        }
